cending by count. Standard first-look at a categorical column."},{"id":"q13_d2","kind":"code","topic":"GroupBy top per group","text":"For each `customer_id`, get the row with the max `amount`. Use .idxmax + .loc.","language":"python","starter":"","solution":"df.loc[df.groupby('customer_id')['amount'].idxmax()]","accept":[{}],"explain":".idxmax returns the index of the max within each group. .loc[indexes] then fetches the actual rows. "Top 1 per group" pattern."},{"id":"q14","kind":"code","topic":"Write CSV","text":"Save `df` to 'out.csv' without the row index.","language":"python","starter":"","solution":"df.to_csv('out.csv', index=False)","accept":[{}],"explain":"index=False suppresses the row index column. ALWAYS set it (otherwise CSV has an unnamed first column)."},{"id":"q15","kind":"code","topic":"GroupBy then reset","text":"Group `df` by `category` and sum, then reset_index so the group key becomes a column.","language":"python","starter":"","solution":"df.groupby('category').sum().reset_index()","accept":[{}],"explain":"After groupby+agg, group key is the index. reset_index = move it back to a column. Useful for tools that want a flat table."}],"CR-PYINT/ch5/s3":[{"id":"q1","kind":"code","topic":"Merge on key","text":"Merge DataFrames `orders` and `customers` on column `customer_id`, inner join. Assign to `merged`.","language":"python","starter":"","solution":"merged = orders.merge(customers, on='customer_id')","accept":[{},{}],"explain":"df.merge() is pandas' SQL JOIN. Default is inner. Use how='left'/'right'/'outer' for other types."},{"id":"q2","kind":"code","topic":"Left merge","text":"Same as before but LEFT join (keep all orders even unmatched).","language":"python","starter":"","solution":"merged = orders.merge(customers, on='customer_id', how='left')","accept":[{}],"explain":"Left join keeps all left rows, fills NaN for unmatched right columns. Same semantics as SQL LEFT JOIN."},{"id":"q3","kind":"code","topic":"concat vertical","text":"Stack DataFrames `df1` and `df2` vertically (row-wise). Assign to `combined`.","language":"python","starter":"import pandas as pd
